<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pula</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pola</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pula is a city at the southern tip of the Istrian peninsula in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>. As the Roman colony of Pietas Iulia it gained monuments such as its well-preserved amphitheatre of the 1st century CE. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> it was the main base of the imperial navy, and it is now an important port and tourist centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pula.jpg" alt="Pula" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Orlovic · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pula_Aerial_View.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
